infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One tsconfig switch, opposite outcomes
  desc node ignores exports and skips the .js rule; nodenext resolves the way Node actually runs
  compares
    - label moduleResolution node
      children
        - label Ignores package.json exports
          desc Guesses main/index; resolves paths the package forbids
        - label No .js extension rule
          desc Accepts ./parser that Node ESM rejects at runtime
        - label CJS require-style walk
          desc Climbs node_modules, no import/require condition match
        - label Legacy CJS projects only
          desc The classic ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND trap
    - label moduleResolution nodenext
      children
        - label Honours exports + conditions
          desc Matches import / require / types targets
        - label Requires .js in ESM imports
          desc Write ./parser.js to import parser.ts
        - label ESM or CJS per package type
          desc Follows the package.json type field
        - label Node libraries and apps today
          desc Editor and runtime resolve identically
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
